# Salmon Baked with Asparagus

{ rating="5" image="salmon_baked_with_asparagus.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- In a small bowl, whisk together

  - [ ] [Olive Oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } (~1/4 cup)
  - [ ] 1/8 tsp of [paprika]{ ing="paprika" }
  - [ ] 1/8 tsp [cayenne pepper]{ ing="cayenne-pepper" }
  - [ ] 2/3 Tbsp [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
  - [ ] pinch of [salt]{ ing="salt" }

- [ ] [Salmon filet]{ ing="salmon-filet" }
- [ ] [Tomato]{ ing="tomato" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] (Optional) [Asparagus]{ ing="asparagus" }
- [ ] [Parmesan cheese]{ ing="parmesan-cheese" }
- [ ] [Rosemary]{ ing="rosemary" }
- [ ] [Thyme]{ ing="thyme" }
- [ ] [Oregano]{ ing="oregano" }
- [ ] [Salt and Pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }
- [ ] Could also add [Parsley and/or Basil]{ ing="parsley-and-or-basil" }

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 400F
1. Whisk together the [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } and [lemon juice]{ ing="lemon-juice" }
1. Cover a baking sheet with tin foil and lay out the fish, [asparagus]{ ing="asparagus" }, [tomatoes]{ ing="tomato" }, and/or any other baked items
1. Spread out the [oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } with a spoon and roll to coat
1. Sprinkle on the additional herbs and [cheese]{ ing="parmesan-cheese" }
1. Bake for 15-25 min depending on thickness with most being around 20 min
